description:
Patients with diseases of the lung or pleural tumors;
Patients with benign diseases of the lungs and pleura, as well as with lung and pleural metastases of other primary tumors;
Healthy control subjects from population-based controls from the study region (Einwohnermeldeamt)

"BTLB is one of the three collections of the CRB-HSM biobank. It includes:
- FFPE and crio-preserved tissues  from tumors (mainly breast, lung, colon), whole blood, serum, plasma, nucleic acids, urine, saliva, blood cell fractions;
- DNA from lymphoprolipherative disorders;
- biopsies from abdominal aorta, carotid, safena."

Patients enrolled in this phase 1b/2 trial will be treated with tremelimumab +/- durvalumab +/- paclitaxel (see study protocol for details).

Baseline and on-treatment (C3D1) biopsies site will be collected, aiming for at least 6 patients per study arm. This unique biobank will be created to study the effects of combined tremelimumab +/- paclitaxel +/- durvalumab on the Tumor Micro-Environment (TME) consisting of the following specimens:
•	Archival tissue that has been collected before study enrollment;
•	Baseline and on-treatment biopsies (0, 9 weeks);
•	PBMCs at baseline and on-treatment (0, 5, 9 and 13 weeks); 
•	Serum at baseline and on-treatment (0, 5, 9, 13, 25, 49 weeks).
